                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                        "entry_id": "0f4355a5-1a20-3f63-b934-e9837d622c7a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To rid of fleas."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "96081a55-9b1f-445f-8d0e-173a27f7a517",
                                "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                                "text": "I had to deflea our cat with a flea comb, even though it wears a flea collar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c191ee22-c787-47f7-a1c9-0e9beab902ce",
                                "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                                "text": "The DDT powder does not kill the rats; it merely defleas them and lessens the likelihood of the spread of typhus fever from rat to man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5acf2407-f67e-42c4-aa08-6042ad9ccc79",
                                "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                                "text": "A fine metal flea comb is an added aid in defleaing a cat, especially if you are the type who gains satisfaction from “cracking” fleas caught in the comb, or from trying to drown them in a glass of water!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89114ce7-3f4f-4e41-bed9-8f9c80845444",
                                "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                                "text": "She cares personally for her dogs, feeds them, defleas them, shouts crossly at them when they misbehave."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a7ec125-0f18-41b4-975b-a13eff7c9d96",
                                "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                                "text": "House, kennels, bedding, runs, all have to be defleaed, as well as the dogs. Note: If the dogs have to be wormed, it is wise to postpone any defleaing efforts for three weeks after worming."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "00da8a62-8a7e-409d-82c1-48c93ec319f9",
                                "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                                "text": "I had my own dog, but I also caught every stray dog in the neighborhood, washed and defleaed it, and anointed it with cologne (causing a great rumpus when discovered by one of my sisters from whom the cheap scent had been appropriated)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a60416ba-94ac-4aaf-9ca5-19590887108a",
                                "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                                "text": "I can get her defleaed. That wouldn't be a problem. I can pay for it now that I've got an after-school job. And Mom's a sucker for strays."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "656f58c9-ac64-46e5-ada7-ddb91bcfbcaf",
                                "sense_id": "13f3f343-8e39-3242-aba8-a23c518f7149",
                                "text": "2009, Louis de Bernières, The Death of Miss Agatha Feakes, [originally published in 2009, Notwithstanding], Storycuts, 2011, unnumbered page,\nShe sits in her armchair, and, one by one, she defleas her cats."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
